 customize the font family used to render a reflowable EPUB, by changing the "},{"identifier":"Preferences.md","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"article","role":"article"},"doc://Readium/documentation/Readium/Accessibility":{"url":"\/documentation\/readium\/accessibility","role":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Readium\/documentation\/Readium\/Accessibility","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Some publications declare their accessibility features and limitations as metadata which broadly mirror the "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/www.w3.org\/TR\/epub-a11y-11"},{"type":"text","text":" specification."}],"kind":"article","title":"Accessibility","type":"topic"},"doc://Readium/documentation/Readium/Getting-Started":{"title":"Getting started","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The Readium Swift toolkit enables you to develop reading apps for iOS and iPadOS. It provides built-in support for multiple publication formats such as EPUB, PDF, audiobooks, and comics."}],"role":"article","kind":"article","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/readium\/getting-started","identifier":"doc:\/\/Readium\/documentation\/Readium\/Getting-Started"},"doc://Readium/documentation/Readium/TTS":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/readium\/tts","identifier":"doc:\/\/Readium\/documentation\/Readium\/TTS","abstract":[],"kind":"article","role":"article","title":"Text-to-speech"},"doc://Readium/documentation/Readium":{"title":"Readium","abstract":[{"text":"The Readium Swift Toolkit is a toolkit for ebooks, audiobooks, and comics written in Swift & Kotlin.","type":"text"}],"kind":"article","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Readium\/documentation\/Readium","role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/readium"},"doc://Readium/documentation/Readium/Preferences":{"title":"Configuring the Navigator","identifier":"doc:\/\/Readium\/documentation\/Readium\/Preferences","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Take a look at the "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"..\/Migration%20Guide.md","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" if you are already using the legacy EPUB settings."}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/readium\/preferences","kind":"article","role":"article"},"doc://Readium/documentation/Readium/Navigator":{"role":"article","url":"\/documentation\/readium\/navigator","title":"Navigator","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"You can use a Readium Navigator to present the publication to the user. The "},{"code":"Navigator","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" renders resources on the screen and offers APIs and user interactions for navigating the contents."}],"kind":"article","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Readium\/documentation\/Readium\/Navigator"},"https://www.edrlab.org/readium-lcp/":{"type":"link","identifier":"https:\/\/www.edrlab.org\/readium-lcp\/","title":"Readium LCP","url":"https:\/\/www.edrlab.org\/readium-lcp\/","titleInlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Readium LCP"}]},"https://www.w3.org/TR/epub-a11y-11":{"titleInlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"EPUB Accessibility"}],"url":"https:\/\/www.w3.org\/TR\/epub-a11y-11","type":"link","identifier":"https:\/\/www.w3.org\/TR\/epub-a11y-11","title":"EPUB Accessibility"},"Preferences.md":{"type":"link","identifier":"Preferences.md","title":"EPUB navigator preferences","url":"Preferences.md","titleInlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"EPUB navigator preferences"}]},"doc://Readium/documentation/Readium/Readium-LCP":{"role":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Readium\/documentation\/Readium\/Readium-LCP","kind":"article","abstract":[{"text":"You can use the Readium Swift toolkit to download and read publications that are protected with the ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/www.edrlab.org\/readium-lcp\/","type":"reference"},{"text":" DRM.","type":"text"}],"title":"Supporting Readium LCP","url":"\/documentation\/readium\/readium-lcp","type":"topic"},"doc://Readium/documentation/Readium/Input":{"title":"Observing user input","kind":"article","url":"\/documentation\/readium\/input","role":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Readium\/documentation\/Readium\/Input","abstract":[{"text":"In visual publications like EPUB or PDF, users can interact with the ","type":"text"},{"code":"VisualNavigator","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" instance using gestures, a keyboard, a mouse, a pencil, or a trackpad. When the publication does not override user input events, you may want to intercept them to trigger actions in your user interface. For example, you can turn pages or toggle the navigation bar on taps, or open a bookmarks screen when pressing the Command-Shift-D hotkey.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic"},"doc://Readium/documentation/Readium/Search":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The Search API lets you look for a textual query in the content of a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Publication"},{"type":"text","text":". EPUB and PDF publications are supported."}],"url":"\/documentation\/readium\/search","kind":"article","title":"Searching a publication","identifier":"doc:\/\/Readium\/documentation\/Readium\/Search","type":"topic","role":"article"},"doc://Readium/documentation/Readium/Migration-Guide":{"role":"article","type":"topic","title":"Migration Guide","kind":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"All migration steps necessary in reading apps to upgrade to major versions of the Swift Readium toolkit will be documented in this file."}],"url":"\/documentation\/readium\/migration-guide","identifier":"doc:\/\/Readium\/documentation\/Readium\/Migration-Guide"},"doc://Readium/documentation/Readium/SwiftUI":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The Navigator is built with UIKit and provides "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"UIViewController"},{"type":"text","text":" implementations. Nevertheless, you can integrate them into a SwiftUI view hierarchy using Apple’s "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/developer.apple.com\/documentation\/swiftui\/uiviewrepresentable"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"topic","title":"Integrating the Navigator with SwiftUI","url":"\/documentation\/readium\/swiftui","identifier":"doc:\/\/Readium\/documentation\/Readium\/SwiftUI","role":"article","kind":"article"},"doc://Readium/documentation/Readium/Open-Publication":{"title":"Opening a publication","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"To open a publication with Readium, you need to instantiate a couple of components: an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AssetRetriever"},{"type":"text","text":" and a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PublicationOpener"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Readium\/documentation\/Readium\/Open-Publication","role":"article","url":"\/documentation\/readium\/open-publication"},"doc://Readium/documentation/Readium/Highlights":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Readium\/documentation\/Readium\/Highlights","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Highlighting lets users mark up passages in a publication for later reference - a core feature of any reading app. In Readium, highlights are built on top of the "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Decoration API"}]},{"type":"text","text":". If you want to understand that API in depth or build a custom decoration style, see the "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"Decorations.md"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"article","url":"\/documentation\/readium\/highlights","role":"article","title":"Implementing Highlights"},"doc://Readium/documentation/Readium/EPUB-Image-Preview":{"title":"EPUB Image Preview","type":"topic","kind":"article","abstract":[{"text":"This guide explains how to detect when a user taps an image in an EPUB publication to present it in a dedicated view, using the ","type":"text"},{"code":"PointerEvent.targetElement","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" API.","type":"text"}],"role":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Readium\/documentation\/Readium\/EPUB-Image-Preview","url":"\/documentation\/readium\/epub-image-preview"},"https://developer.apple.com/documentation/swiftui/uiviewrepresentable":{"titleInlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"UIViewRepresentable"}],"url":"https:\/\/developer.apple.com\/documentation\/swiftui\/uiviewrepresentable","type":"link","identifier":"https:\/\/developer.apple.com\/documentation\/swiftui\/uiviewrepresentable","title":"UIViewRepresentable"},"doc://Readium/documentation/Readium/Decorations":{"title":"Decorations","identifier":"doc:\/\/Readium\/documentation\/Readium\/Decorations","url":"\/documentation\/readium\/decorations","kind":"article","role":"article","abstract":[{"text":"The Decoration API lets you overlay visual elements on publication content – highlights, search result markers, TTS playback indicators, page-number labels in the margin, and more. For the common case of implementing user highlights, see the ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"Highlights.md"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"topic"},"doc://Readium/documentation/Readium/Content":{"type":"topic","abstract":[],"url":"\/documentation\/readium\/content","role":"article","title":"Extracting the content of a publication","kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Readium\/documentation\/Readium\/Content"},"Highlights.md":{"type":"link","identifier":"Highlights.md","title":"Highlighting guide","url":"Highlights.md","titleInlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Highlighting guide"}]},"Decorations.md":{"titleInlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Decorations guide"}],"url":"Decorations.md","type":"link","identifier":"Decorations.md","title":"Decorations guide"}}}